<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<model version="NetLogo 7.0.4" snapToGrid="true">
  <code><![CDATA[;; Stage 4: add purchase, transport, and relationship costs.
;; Positions show the network; transport rates belong to supplier-buyer pairs.
;; Inventory, disruptions, and changing prices come in later stages.

breed [suppliers supplier]
breed [manufacturers manufacturer]
directed-link-breed [contracts contract]

globals [
  capacity-setting
  demand-min-setting
  demand-max-setting
  partner-count-setting
  route-seed-setting
  settings-ready?
  active-capacity
  active-demand-min
  active-demand-max
  active-partner-count
  active-route-seed
  route-rates
  relationship-fee
  period-demand
  period-delivered
  period-unmet
  cumulative-demand
  cumulative-delivered
  cumulative-unmet
  period-purchase-cost
  period-transport-cost
  period-relationship-cost
  period-total-cost
  cumulative-purchase-cost
  cumulative-transport-cost
  cumulative-relationship-cost
  cumulative-total-cost
]

suppliers-own [
  capacity
  orders-received
  amount-shipped
  fill-ratio
  unit-price
]

contracts-own [
  units-ordered
  units-delivered
  transport-rate
  purchase-charge
  transport-charge
]

manufacturers-own [
  demand
  order-quantity
  amount-received
  unmet-demand
  buyer-purchase-cost
  buyer-transport-cost
  buyer-relationship-cost
  buyer-total-cost
  buyer-cumulative-cost
]

to startup
  reset-parameters
end

to reset-parameters
  set capacity-setting 50
  set demand-min-setting 30
  set demand-max-setting 50
  set partner-count-setting 1
  set route-seed-setting 2026
  set settings-ready? true
end

to ensure-settings
  if settings-ready? != true [ reset-parameters ]
end

to read-interface-settings
  set capacity-setting runresult "supplier-capacity"
  set demand-min-setting runresult "min-demand"
  set demand-max-setting runresult "max-demand"
  set partner-count-setting runresult "supplier-count"
  set route-seed-setting runresult "route-seed"
end

to setup
  ensure-settings
  read-interface-settings
  if demand-min-setting > demand-max-setting [
    error "Minimum demand exceeds maximum demand. Change the sliders before Setup."
  ]
  ;; Preserve control values because clear-all resets model globals.
  let selected-capacity capacity-setting
  let selected-min demand-min-setting
  let selected-max demand-max-setting
  let selected-partners partner-count-setting
  let selected-route-seed route-seed-setting
  clear-all
  set capacity-setting selected-capacity
  set demand-min-setting selected-min
  set demand-max-setting selected-max
  set partner-count-setting selected-partners
  set route-seed-setting selected-route-seed
  set settings-ready? true
  set active-capacity selected-capacity
  set active-demand-min selected-min
  set active-demand-max selected-max
  set active-partner-count selected-partners
  set active-route-seed selected-route-seed
  set relationship-fee 50
  ask patches [ set pcolor (rgb 17 27 43) ]

  ;; Fixed positions keep the procurement links easy to follow.
  create-suppliers 3 [
    setxy -10 (10 - who * 10)
    set shape "box"
    set size 3
    set color (rgb 46 196 168)
    set label (word "S" (who + 1))
    set label-color white
    set capacity capacity-setting
    set orders-received 0
    set amount-shipped 0
    set fill-ratio 1
    set unit-price 100
  ]

  create-manufacturers 3 [
    let index (who - 3)
    setxy 10 (10 - index * 10)
    set shape "house"
    set size 2.8
    set color (rgb 100 160 245)
    set label-color white
    ;; Draw demand once per manufacturer; it stays fixed during this run.
    set demand demand-min-setting +
      random (demand-max-setting - demand-min-setting + 1)
    set label (word "M" (index + 1) "  0/" demand)
    set order-quantity 0
    set amount-received 0
    set unmet-demand 0
    set buyer-purchase-cost 0
    set buyer-transport-cost 0
    set buyer-relationship-cost 0
    set buyer-total-cost 0
    set buyer-cumulative-cost 0
  ]

  ;; Sample all nine potential route rates with a separate, fixed seed.
  ;; This keeps transport conditions identical across sourcing strategies.
  with-local-randomness [
    random-seed route-seed-setting
    set route-rates n-values 3 [
      n-values 3 [ precision (0.5 + random-float 1) 2 ]
    ]
  ]

  ;; Fixed preference lists make the three strategies easy to compare.
  ;; The first supplier preserves the previous stage's links.
  let supplier-list sort suppliers
  ask manufacturers [
    let index (who - 3)
    let preferences item index [[0 1 2] [1 2 0] [0 2 1]]
    foreach (sublist preferences 0 partner-count-setting) [ supplier-index ->
      create-contract-to (item supplier-index supplier-list) [
        set color (rgb 85 112 139)
        set thickness 0.12
        set units-ordered 0
        set units-delivered 0
        set transport-rate item supplier-index (item index route-rates)
        set purchase-charge 0
        set transport-charge 0
      ]
    ]
  ]

  set period-demand 0
  set period-delivered 0
  set period-unmet 0
  set cumulative-demand 0
  set cumulative-delivered 0
  set cumulative-unmet 0
  set period-purchase-cost 0
  set period-transport-cost 0
  set period-relationship-cost 0
  set period-total-cost 0
  set cumulative-purchase-cost 0
  set cumulative-transport-cost 0
  set cumulative-relationship-cost 0
  set cumulative-total-cost 0
  reset-ticks
end

to go
  if not any? manufacturers [
    error "Run Setup before Step or Run."
  ]
  read-interface-settings
  if demand-min-setting > demand-max-setting [
    error "Minimum demand exceeds maximum demand. Change the sliders and run Setup."
  ]
  if capacity-setting != active-capacity or
     demand-min-setting != active-demand-min or
     demand-max-setting != active-demand-max or
     partner-count-setting != active-partner-count or
     route-seed-setting != active-route-seed [
    error "A slider changed. Run Setup before Step or Run."
  ]

  ;; 1. Split each manufacturer's full demand equally across its links.
  ask suppliers [
    set orders-received 0
    set amount-shipped 0
  ]
  ask manufacturers [
    set order-quantity demand
    set amount-received 0
    set unmet-demand 0
  ]
  ask contracts [
    set units-ordered [order-quantity] of end1 / [count my-out-contracts] of end1
    set units-delivered 0
  ]

  ;; 2. Each supplier allocates capacity proportionally across its links.
  ask suppliers [
    set orders-received sum [units-ordered] of my-in-contracts
    ifelse orders-received = 0
      [ set fill-ratio 1 ]
      [ set fill-ratio min (list 1 (capacity / orders-received)) ]
  ]

  ;; 3. Deliver each link's order at its supplier's fill ratio.
  ask contracts [
    set units-delivered units-ordered * [fill-ratio] of end2
    set purchase-charge units-delivered * [unit-price] of end2
    set transport-charge units-delivered * transport-rate
    ifelse units-delivered < units-ordered
      [ set color (rgb 250 166 79) ]
      [ set color (rgb 85 112 139) ]
  ]

  ask manufacturers [
    set amount-received sum [units-delivered] of my-out-contracts
    set unmet-demand max (list 0 (demand - amount-received))
    set buyer-purchase-cost sum [purchase-charge] of my-out-contracts
    set buyer-transport-cost sum [transport-charge] of my-out-contracts
    set buyer-relationship-cost relationship-fee * count my-out-contracts
    set buyer-total-cost buyer-purchase-cost + buyer-transport-cost + buyer-relationship-cost
    set buyer-cumulative-cost buyer-cumulative-cost + buyer-total-cost
    ifelse unmet-demand > 0
      [ set color (rgb 250 166 79) ]
      [ set color (rgb 100 160 245) ]
    set label (word "M" (who - 2) "  " (precision amount-received 1) "/" demand)
  ]

  ask suppliers [
    set amount-shipped sum [units-delivered] of my-in-contracts
    ifelse orders-received > capacity
      [ set color (rgb 250 166 79) ]
      [ set color (rgb 46 196 168) ]
    set label (word "S" (who + 1) "  " orders-received "→" (precision amount-shipped 1))
  ]

  ;; 4. Update demand and cost totals. One tick is one procurement cycle.
  set period-demand sum [demand] of manufacturers
  set period-delivered sum [amount-received] of manufacturers
  set period-unmet sum [unmet-demand] of manufacturers
  set cumulative-demand cumulative-demand + period-demand
  set cumulative-delivered cumulative-delivered + period-delivered
  set cumulative-unmet cumulative-unmet + period-unmet
  set period-purchase-cost sum [buyer-purchase-cost] of manufacturers
  set period-transport-cost sum [buyer-transport-cost] of manufacturers
  set period-relationship-cost sum [buyer-relationship-cost] of manufacturers
  set period-total-cost period-purchase-cost + period-transport-cost + period-relationship-cost
  set cumulative-purchase-cost cumulative-purchase-cost + period-purchase-cost
  set cumulative-transport-cost cumulative-transport-cost + period-transport-cost
  set cumulative-relationship-cost cumulative-relationship-cost + period-relationship-cost
  set cumulative-total-cost cumulative-total-cost + period-total-cost
  tick
end

to-report period-fulfillment-text
  if period-demand = 0 [ report "N/A" ]
  report (word (precision (100 * period-delivered / period-demand) 1) "%")
end

to-report cumulative-fulfillment-text
  if cumulative-demand = 0 [ report "N/A" ]
  report (word (precision (100 * cumulative-delivered / cumulative-demand) 1) "%")
end]]></code>
  <widgets>
    <view x="260" wrappingAllowedX="false" y="78" frameRate="20.0" minPycor="-16" height="500" showTickCounter="true" patchSize="15.0" fontSize="11" wrappingAllowedY="false" width="500" tickCounterLabel="Cycle" maxPycor="16" updateMode="1" maxPxcor="16" minPxcor="-16"></view>
    <note x="20" y="12" backgroundDark="0" fontSize="18" width="1060" markdown="false" height="50" textColorDark="-1" textColorLight="-16777216" backgroundLight="0">Critical Mineral Procurement | Stage 4</note>
    <note x="20" y="72" backgroundDark="0" fontSize="11" width="220" markdown="false" height="38" textColorDark="-1" textColorLight="-16777216" backgroundLight="0">Capacity, sourcing, and procurement costs</note>
    <note x="20" y="128" backgroundDark="0" fontSize="13" width="220" markdown="false" height="32" textColorDark="-1" textColorLight="-16777216" backgroundLight="0">Controls</note>
    <button x="20" y="168" height="46" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="220" display="Setup">setup</button>
    <button x="20" y="224" height="46" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="105" display="Step">go</button>
    <button x="135" y="224" height="46" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="true" kind="Observer" width="105" display="Run">go</button>
    <note x="20" y="278" backgroundDark="0" fontSize="10" width="220" markdown="false" height="22" textColorDark="-1" textColorLight="-16777216" backgroundLight="0">Suppliers per manufacturer</note>
    <slider x="20" step="1.0" y="302" max="3.0" width="220" display="supplier-count" height="55" min="1.0" direction="Horizontal" default="1.0" variable="supplier-count" units="suppliers"></slider>
    <slider x="20" step="10.0" y="360" max="100.0" width="220" display="supplier-capacity" height="55" min="0.0" direction="Horizontal" default="50.0" variable="supplier-capacity" units="units"></slider>
    <slider x="20" step="10.0" y="418" max="100.0" width="220" display="min-demand" height="55" min="0.0" direction="Horizontal" default="30.0" variable="min-demand" units="units"></slider>
    <slider x="20" step="10.0" y="476" max="100.0" width="220" display="max-demand" height="55" min="0.0" direction="Horizontal" default="50.0" variable="max-demand" units="units"></slider>
    <note x="20" y="590" backgroundDark="0" fontSize="10" width="220" markdown="false" height="22" textColorDark="-1" textColorLight="-16777216" backgroundLight="0">Transport cost scenario</note>
    <slider x="20" step="1.0" y="614" max="9999.0" width="220" display="route-seed" height="55" min="1.0" direction="Horizontal" default="2026.0" variable="route-seed"></slider>
    <note x="20" y="684" backgroundDark="0" fontSize="10" width="220" markdown="false" height="34" textColorDark="-1" textColorLight="-16777216" backgroundLight="0">After changing a slider, click Setup.</note>
    <note x="780" y="83" backgroundDark="0" fontSize="14" width="300" markdown="false" height="31" textColorDark="-1" textColorLight="-16777216" backgroundLight="0">Network totals</note>
    <monitor x="780" precision="0" y="122" height="62" fontSize="12" width="143" display="Period demand">period-demand</monitor>
    <monitor x="937" precision="0" y="122" height="62" fontSize="12" width="143" display="Period delivered">period-delivered</monitor>
    <monitor x="780" precision="0" y="194" height="62" fontSize="12" width="143" display="Period unmet">period-unmet</monitor>
    <monitor x="937" precision="0" y="194" height="62" fontSize="12" width="143" display="Period fill rate">period-fulfillment-text</monitor>
    <monitor x="780" precision="0" y="266" height="62" fontSize="12" width="143" display="Total unmet">cumulative-unmet</monitor>
    <monitor x="937" precision="0" y="266" height="62" fontSize="12" width="143" display="Overall fill rate">cumulative-fulfillment-text</monitor>
    <plot x="780" autoPlotX="true" yMax="100.0" autoPlotY="true" yAxis="Units" y="346" xMin="0.0" height="231" legend="true" xMax="20.0" yMin="0.0" width="300" xAxis="Cycle" display="Demand and deliveries per cycle">
      <setup></setup>
      <update></update>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="Demand" color="-16736752" legend="true"><setup></setup><update>plot period-demand</update></pen>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="Delivered" color="-12015457" legend="true"><setup></setup><update>plot period-delivered</update></pen>
    </plot>
    <note x="780" y="592" backgroundDark="0" fontSize="13" width="300" markdown="false" height="29" textColorDark="-1" textColorLight="-16777216" backgroundLight="0">Procurement costs</note>
    <monitor x="780" precision="2" y="628" height="62" fontSize="11" width="94" display="Purchase">period-purchase-cost</monitor>
    <monitor x="883" precision="2" y="628" height="62" fontSize="11" width="94" display="Transport">period-transport-cost</monitor>
    <monitor x="986" precision="2" y="628" height="62" fontSize="11" width="94" display="Link fees">period-relationship-cost</monitor>
    <monitor x="780" precision="2" y="700" height="62" fontSize="12" width="143" display="Period total">period-total-cost</monitor>
    <monitor x="937" precision="2" y="700" height="62" fontSize="12" width="143" display="Cumulative total">cumulative-total-cost</monitor>
  </widgets>
  <info><![CDATA[## Purpose

Stage 4 adds three cost components to the capacity-constrained procurement network: mineral purchases, transportation, and the upkeep of supplier relationships. The network still has three suppliers and three manufacturers. Each manufacturer splits its order equally among one, two, or three fixed suppliers. Inventory, disruptions, supplier switching, and changing prices come later.

## Network and controls

The supplier-count slider sets the number of suppliers used by *each* manufacturer. Setup selects the first one, two, or three suppliers in these fixed preference lists:

| Manufacturer | First | Second | Third |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| M1 | S1 | S2 | S3 |
| M2 | S2 | S3 | S1 |
| M3 | S1 | S3 | S2 |

The supplier-capacity slider sets each supplier's capacity. The min-demand and max-demand sliders give all manufacturers the same inclusive demand range; Setup draws one integer demand per manufacturer. Demand, capacity, and relationships stay fixed during a run. Set min-demand equal to max-demand when you want the same demand in repeated strategy comparisons.

Positions are fixed for readability and have no effect on transportation cost. Each potential manufacturer–supplier pair instead has a unit transportation rate. Setup draws all nine rates from 0.5–1.5 cost units per delivered mineral unit, rounded to two decimal places. The route-seed slider (1–9999) selects a reproducible rate table. The same seed produces the same rates for all three sourcing strategies, including pairs without an active link. Changing the seed and clicking Setup generates a different scenario. The rate table stays fixed during a run.

## Each cycle

1. Each manufacturer splits its full demand equally among its contract links.
2. Each supplier fills those orders up to its capacity, using the same fill ratio for every incoming link.
3. A link's purchase charge is its delivered units × the supplier's unit price. Its transport charge is delivered units × that pair's transport rate. Both charges are zero when nothing is delivered.
4. Each manufacturer also pays 50 cost units per active supplier relationship every cycle, even if that supplier delivers nothing. Its total cost is purchase + transport + relationship cost.
5. The model updates current-cycle and cumulative cost and demand totals. One tick is one procurement cycle.

Every supplier's unit purchase price is 100 cost units in this stage. Supplier-specific prices and price feedback are later stages. Unmet demand is reported separately; it is not assigned a monetary penalty.

## Reading the display

Click Setup to build the network, Step for one cycle, or Run for continuous cycles. Changing any slider requires another Setup. If min-demand exceeds max-demand, Setup and subsequent cycles stop with an error.

Green boxes are suppliers; blue houses are manufacturers. Orange suppliers received more orders than their capacity; orange manufacturers have unmet demand. An orange link was not fully delivered. Supplier labels show `orders received → amount shipped`; manufacturer labels show `amount received / demand`.

The upper right monitors show period demand, deliveries, unmet demand, and fill rates. The lower right monitors show current-cycle purchase, transport, and relationship charges, their period total, and the cumulative total across completed cycles. Fill rate is delivered / demand × 100%; it shows N/A when demand is zero.

## Hand-check example

Set supplier-capacity to 50, min-demand and max-demand to 30, and route-seed to 2026. The route rates, with manufacturers as rows and suppliers as columns, are:

| Route | S1 | S2 | S3 |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| M1 | 0.72 | 0.91 | 1.48 |
| M2 | 0.59 | 0.98 | 1.49 |
| M3 | 0.70 | 1.41 | 1.06 |

With supplier-count = 1, S1 ships 50 and S2 ships 30, for 80 delivered and 10 unmet. Purchase cost is 8,000, transport cost is 64.90, and three relationship fees total 150, so period total cost is 8,214.90. With supplier-count = 2, all 90 units are delivered; purchase, transport, and relationship costs are 9,000, 87.90, and 300, for a period total of 9,387.90. With supplier-count = 3, all 90 units are delivered and the three costs are 9,000, 93.40, and 450, for a period total of 9,543.40.]]></info>
